  "description": "Proposed single-storey side and rear extensions",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-203e1e43-7fff-ffa3-5226-16e9835fe384&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its unsympathetic scale, bulk, location and detailed design, would comprise an incongruous, discordant and overly-prominent form of development, which would fail to conserve or enhance the significance of the locally listed application site, adjoining locally listed terrace and the setting of the adjacent Grade II listed Chalmar House. As such the proposed development is considered contrary to policy D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering Good Design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan 2021, policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) and LP4 (Non Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and the NPPF.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
